PROMPT_CASE_RUN review status=Completed error=None result=Some("Verified the review against the source; both findings check out against `src/limit.rs` as read directly. No files were changed.\n\n## Findings\n\n**1. High — Off-by-one: returns 4 lines, not 3** (`src/limit.rs:3`)\n\n```rust\n(0..=MAX_LINES).map(|i| lines[i].to_string()).collect()\n```\n\nWith `MAX_LINES = 3` (line 1), the inclusive range `0..=MAX_LINES` yields `0,1,2,3` — four indices. The function always returns 4 elements when it returns at all. Concrete failure: `first_lines(&[\"a\",\"b\",\"c\",\"d\"])` returns `[\"a\",\"b\",\"c\",\"d\"]`, violating the `MAX_LINES` contract. Smallest fix: use the exclusive range `0..MAX_LINES`, or better, address finding 2's fix which covers both.\n\n**2. High — Reachable panic on valid input: index out of bounds** (`src/limit.rs:3`)\n\nThe same line indexes `lines[i]` unconditionally with a fixed 4-element range, independent of `lines.len()`. Any slice shorter than 4 panics — short slices are ordinary, valid `&[&str]` values. Concrete failures:\n- `first_lines(&[])` → panic, index 0, len 0\n- `first_lines(&[\"a\"])` → panic, index 1, len 1\n- `first_lines(&[\"a\",\"b\",\"c\"])` → panic, index 3, len 3 — this is exactly the input the constant implies should succeed\n\nSmallest fix that resolves both findings: `lines.iter().take(MAX_LINES).map(|s| s.to_string()).collect()`. If hard failure on short input is intended instead, it should be an explicit `Result`, not a panic.\n\n## Non-issues checked\n\n- No integer type mismatch: `MAX_LINES` is `usize`, matching slice indexing.\n- No overflow: `RangeInclusive` never computes `MAX_LINES + 1`, and the value is small.\n- No state, so no re-entrancy or race surface; `&str -> String` loses no data.\n\n## Coverage limits\n\n- The workspace has **no callers and no tests** for `first_lines`/`MAX_LINES` (workspace-wide search matched only the definition; no `main.rs`/`lib.rs`/`tests/`), so the intended contract for short input (truncate vs. require vs. error) could not be confirmed from a call site; the fix above assumes truncation.\n- Compiler confirmation was unavailable; the analysis is from slice-indexing semantics, and the three inputs listed above would reproduce finding 2 immediately under `cargo test`.\n\n**Result: review complete (2 actionable findings), no modifications made.**")
